   "rule": "C; **required when, and only when, the site-local calendar date of `event_datetime` equals the known `discharge_date` of the parent procedure and the event is after `procedure_end_datetime`.** NOT_APPLICABLE in every other case, including an event on an earlier or later date, an intraprocedural event, and an event whose discharge date is not yet known. This is the one lean conditional fact that separates the two same-day states; **no discharge time is collected**, because a discharge timestamp would be a new required value on every admitted case to answer a question that arises only on the discharge day itself. INDETERMINATE is a legitimate recorded value where the record genuinely does not establish the order; it is never treated as BEFORE_DISCHARGE"
